Subject: Allow clients to release their own sensor claims after locking

GNOME releases ambient-light sensors as its session becomes inactive. Checking
the claim Polkit action again rejects that cleanup and leaves polling enabled.
Keep authorization for all new claims. Release still uses the unique D-Bus
sender's own hash-table entry; an unrelated sender cannot release another
client's claim. Unknown methods continue to fail before dispatch.

Applies to the hash-pinned Ubuntu iio-sensor-proxy 3.5 source (GPL-3.0-only).

--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -541,7 +541,10 @@
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (!check_claim_permission (data, sender, &error)) {
+	/* Releasing an existing per-sender claim must work after session lock.
+	 * client_release() cannot remove another sender's ownership. */
+	if (g_str_has_prefix (method_name, "Claim") &&
+	    !check_claim_permission (data, sender, &error)) {
 		g_dbus_method_invocation_return_gerror (invocation, error);
 		return;
 	}
